    link "Training Course: Digital Accessibility Foundations The free \"Introduction to Web Accessibility\" online course provides the foundation you need to make your digital technology accessible. It's designed for: technical and non-technical learners developers, designers, ux, writers, managers, advocates professionals, instructors, students About the Free Online Course" https://www.w3.org/WAI/fundamentals/foundations-course/ @424,1620,287,203
    h2 Web Accessibility Perspectives: Video Captions @424,1835,287,43
    text Captions are the audio information in text that is synchronized with the audio and visual content. Captions are called "subtitles" in some regions. @424,1890,287,81
    text Video Captions are essential for people with disabilities and benefit everyone in a variety of situations. @424,1983,287,61
    row @424,2056,287,41
